{
  "html": "<p>First reference<sup><a href=\"#user-content-fn-b\" id=\"user-content-fnref-b\" data-footnote-ref=\"\" aria-describedby=\"footnote-label\">1</a></sup> establishes footnote b as number one.</p><p>Footnote a<sup><a href=\"#user-content-fn-a\" id=\"user-content-fnref-a\" data-footnote-ref=\"\" aria-describedby=\"footnote-label\">2</a></sup> is defined first in source order, but is referenced second, so it becomes number two.</p><p>A second reference to footnote b<sup><a href=\"#user-content-fn-b\" id=\"user-content-fnref-b-1\" data-footnote-ref=\"\" aria-describedby=\"footnote-label\">1</a></sup> shares its number but gets its own backreference id.</p><p>An empty-looking label<sup><a href=\"#user-content-fn-3\" id=\"user-content-fnref-3\" data-footnote-ref=\"\" aria-describedby=\"footnote-label\">3</a></sup> falls back to a numeric id.</p><p>Duplicate definitions collapse: the first one wins.</p><section data-footnotes=\"\" class=\"footnotes\"><div role=\"heading\" aria-level=\"2\" class=\"sr-only\" style=\"position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;padding:0;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);clip-path:inset(50%);white-space:nowrap;border:0\" id=\"footnote-label\">Footnotes</div><ol><li id=\"user-content-fn-b\"><p>Definition for b, but referenced first in the document.</p><a href=\"#user-content-fnref-b\" data-footnote-backref=\"\" aria-label=\"Back to reference 1\">↩</a><a href=\"#user-content-fnref-b-1\" data-footnote-backref=\"\" aria-label=\"Back to reference 1-2\">↩</a></li><li id=\"user-content-fn-a\"><p>Definition for a, defined first in source order.</p><a href=\"#user-content-fnref-a\" data-footnote-backref=\"\" aria-label=\"Back to reference 2\">↩</a></li><li id=\"user-content-fn-3\"><p>A label that slugifies to nothing.</p><a href=\"#user-content-fnref-3\" data-footnote-backref=\"\" aria-label=\"Back to reference 3\">↩</a></li></ol></section>",
